{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWrb73xjwbdBkhodJ9Q7oA","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, I found information about **KIP-1333: Support log segments larger than 2 GB** which includes a JIRA issue (KAFKA-20552) and a mailing list discussion initiated by Haifeng Chen.\\\\n\\\\n## Summary\\\\n\\\\n**KIP-1333** proposes to **support log segments larger than 2 GB** in Apache Kafka. The proposal addresses the long-standing limitation where:\\\\n\\\\n- The `log.segment.bytes` configuration is capped at `Integer.MAX_VALUE` (~2 GB)\\\\n- The `.index` file format uses 4-byte signed integers, unable to address beyond ~2 GB\\\\n\\\\n**Key problems this solves:**\\\\n- Excessive file handle usage (a 10 TB partition with 2 GB segments requires ~20,000 open files)\\\\n- Frequent segment rolls (high-throughput workloads rolling segments every ~4 seconds)\\\\n- More log cleaning/compaction work overhead\\\\n- Remote storage overhead for tiered storage operations\\\\n\\\\n**Related JIRA Issue:**\\\\n- **KAFKA-20552**: \\\\\\\"Support log segments larger than 2 GB\\\\\\\" - created by Haifeng Chen on May 5, 2026\\\\n\\\\n**Mailing List Discussion:**\\\\n- Haifeng Chen initiated a [DISCUSS] thread on the dev@kafka.apache.org mailing list on May 5, 2026\\\\n- The thread received feedback from community members like Muralidhar Basani, who raised clarification questions about index file detection, caching mechanisms, and implementation details\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/05/05/jira-13650085-created-bca7f53c.md` (JIRA issue creation)\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/05/05/mail-112a535ad8c4fa1e9928d615-135cfc74.md` (initial mailing list discussion)\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/05/06/jira-13650085-change-23050795-0-4fd36f8f.md` (JIRA issue updates with KIP reference)\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/05/09/mail-58eda815da3da5dd252a9b34-f766bf95.md` (mailing list feedback)\\\"